 make this less likely", "Primary neurological syndrome: non-focal findings with visual acuity changes suggest secondary cause"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.004212282437727, "posterior": 0.004212282437727, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.005567711956988016, "posterior": 0.005567711956988016, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leukemia", "lymphoblastic lymphoma"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3546741812566134, "posterior": 0.3546741812566134, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.046008016701461374, "posterior": 0.046008016701461374, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.008, "danger": 0.4, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2", "B3", "B4"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "What evidence is MOST INCONSISTENT with Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts? Identify the single strongest finding that argues against this diagnosis.", "summary": "No findings decisively contradict B1; all align with myeloid neoplasm."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of 35% blasts in peripheral blood with a normal platelet count argue for CML-BC (B3.1) rather than PMF (B3.4)?", "summary": "35% myeloid blasts in blood with normal platelets are more typical of CML-BC (B3.1) than PMF (B3.4), which often presents with low platelets and marrow fibrosis. This moderately supports B3.1 and weakly argues against B3.4."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset of constitutional symptoms (several days to weeks) with 35% blasts in peripheral blood argue against de novo AML (B1) and favor a chronic process like CML-BC (B3.1)?", "summary": "Subacute constitutional symptoms with blasts are not pathognomonic for CML-BC (B3.1) and are equally plausible in de novo AML (B1). This is neutral for both branches."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of lymphoid blast morphology in blood smear evidence argue against ALL (B2) and confirm myeloid lineage involvement (B1)?", "summary": "Lack of lymphoid blast features confirms myeloid lineage involvement, moderately supporting B1 and strongly arguing against B2 (ALL)."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented splenomegaly or chronic leukocytosis history in the vignette argue against CML-BC (B3.1) and favor de novo AML (B1)?", "summary": "Lack of chronic leukocytosis history makes blast crisis less likely, moderately reducing B3.1's probability while de novo AML (B1) remains plausible."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of splenomegaly or marrow fibrosis evidence in physical exam argue against Primary Myelofibrosis (B3.4) and favor CML-BC (B3.1)?", "summary": "Absence of splenomegaly and marrow fibrosis in physical exam weakly argues against PMF (B3.4), as these are expected in myelofibrosis."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B3", 0.655], ["B3.1", 0.431], ["B4", 0.174]]}, {"top": [["B3", 0.337], ["B3.1", 0.178], ["B3.2", 0.077]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers present", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading hypothesis (B3.1) has posterior 0.178 < 0.75 and dangerous alternatives (B1, B2) with posterior ≥ 0.077 but < 0.10. Further testing (e.g., bone marrow biopsy, flow cytometry, JAK2 mutation analysis) can resolve uncertainty between CML-BC, AML, and other MPN subtypes."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.75, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.17771260062533573, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Myelofibrosis', 'Increased circulating myelocyte count', 'Multiple myeloma'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B3", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.655}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "posterior": 0.355, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": []}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=75%, source=primekg]\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm: bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → pain → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
